==================================================================================================
THE DISCREPANCY ROUTE: L^1 (far) DIVERGES, L^2 (variance) CONVERGES
==================================================================================================

(A) L^1 OBSTRUCTION:  sum_{m=1}^{M} |ahat(m)| = sum |sin(pi m/7)|/(pi m)  DIVERGES ~ (2/pi^2)ln M
    M=    10:  sum|ahat| = 0.59231   (2/pi^2)lnM = 0.46660   -> grows without bound
    M=   100:  sum|ahat| = 1.04252   (2/pi^2)lnM = 0.93320   -> grows without bound
    M=  1000:  sum|ahat| = 1.50158   (2/pi^2)lnM = 1.39980   -> grows without bound
    M= 10000:  sum|ahat| = 1.96015   (2/pi^2)lnM = 1.86641   -> grows without bound
    M=100000:  sum|ahat| = 2.41887   (2/pi^2)lnM = 2.33301   -> grows without bound
    => sum|ahat(m)| = +inf: the arc indicator is BV but not absolutely Fourier-summable,
       so any term-by-term ABSOLUTE bound on a product of arcs DIVERGES. Cancellation is mandatory.
    CONTRAST (L^2, Parseval):  sum_{m!=0}|ahat(m)|^2 = theta(1-theta) = 6/49 = 0.12245  (FINITE)
       numerically sum_{m=1}^{2e5} |ahat|^2 = 0.12245  (x2 for +-m) -> 6/49

(B) L^2 CONVERGENCE:  Var(W) = sum_{nu!=0} |What(nu)|^2  converges in (Mmax,Smax) -> Var_exact
  Sidon-5 [0,1,3,7,12]:  Var_exact = 7.890380e-03
      Mmax=2 Smax=4:  sum|What|^2 = 6.105363e-03   ratio=0.7738
      Mmax=3 Smax=4:  sum|What|^2 = 7.823100e-03   ratio=0.9915
      Mmax=3 Smax=5:  sum|What|^2 = 7.609430e-03   ratio=0.9644
      Mmax=4 Smax=5:  sum|What|^2 = 8.022392e-03   ratio=1.0167
  block-6 [0..5] (compact):  Var_exact = 3.276783e-02
      Mmax=2 Smax=4:  sum|What|^2 = 2.620531e-02   ratio=0.7997
      Mmax=3 Smax=4:  sum|What|^2 = 3.431957e-02   ratio=1.0474
      Mmax=3 Smax=6:  sum|What|^2 = 3.072650e-02   ratio=0.9377
      Mmax=4 Smax=6:  sum|What|^2 = 3.385291e-02   ratio=1.0331
  spread-6 [0,1,3,7,12,20]:  Var_exact = 7.258757e-03
      Mmax=2 Smax=4:  sum|What|^2 = 6.479984e-03   ratio=0.8927
      Mmax=3 Smax=4:  sum|What|^2 = 8.098652e-03   ratio=1.1157
      Mmax=3 Smax=6:  sum|What|^2 = 7.291401e-03   ratio=1.0045
      Mmax=4 Smax=6:  sum|What|^2 = 7.337157e-03   ratio=1.0108
  spread-7 [0,1,3,7,12,20,30]:  Var_exact = 8.298172e-03
      Mmax=2 Smax=4:  sum|What|^2 = 7.420499e-03   ratio=0.8942
      Mmax=3 Smax=4:  sum|What|^2 = 1.012131e-02   ratio=1.2197
      Mmax=3 Smax=6:  sum|What|^2 = 8.350657e-03   ratio=1.0063
      Mmax=4 Smax=6:  sum|What|^2 = 8.306487e-03   ratio=1.0010
    => the L^2 variance sum CONVERGES (ratio->1), UNLIKE the L^1 far bound (PHI->inf).
       This is the correct convergent object for the discrepancy route.

(C) LOW-FREQUENCY / ADDITIVE-ENERGY DOMINANCE of Var(W) = sum_nu |What(nu)|^2:
  block-6: top-|What(nu)|^2 by nu (nu = m.e, smallest = single differences):
      nu=   2: |What|^2=5.497e-03  (16.2% of Var)
      nu=  -2: |What|^2=5.497e-03  (16.2% of Var)
      nu=  -4: |What|^2=3.383e-03  (10.0% of Var)
      nu=   4: |What|^2=3.383e-03  (10.0% of Var)
      nu=   3: |What|^2=2.977e-03  (8.8% of Var)
      nu=  -3: |What|^2=2.977e-03  (8.8% of Var)
  spread-6: top-|What(nu)|^2 by nu (nu = m.e, smallest = single differences):
      nu=  12: |What|^2=8.557e-04  (11.7% of Var)
      nu= -12: |What|^2=8.557e-04  (11.7% of Var)
      nu=   6: |What|^2=3.951e-04  (5.4% of Var)
      nu=  -6: |What|^2=3.951e-04  (5.4% of Var)
      nu=   4: |What|^2=3.171e-04  (4.3% of Var)
      nu=  -4: |What|^2=3.171e-04  (4.3% of Var)
    => Var is dominated by nu = SMALL DIFFERENCES; multiplicities = additive energy (klein THM-656).
==================================================================================================
